From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:52:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pan/layout: leave a cache line of slack after 24/96-bit
 images

OpenCL-CTS image reads of CL_RGB images (RGB8 UNORM/SNORM 2D arrays,
RGB32I 3D) fault intermittently on Mali-G31 (Bifrost v7.0):
"Unhandled Page fault in AS0 at VA 0x...000", JOB_BUS_FAULT on the
compute slot, the remaining work-items never store. The fault address
is page aligned every time and the formats that fault are exactly the
non-power-of-two texel sizes; RGBA and the other formats with the same
kernels and sizes never fault. The images that fault have data that
ends exactly on a page boundary (21x32x14 RGB8: row 64, layer 2048,
28672 bytes; 25x128x32 RGB32I: row 320, slice 40960, 0x140000 bytes)
and the random integer coordinates clamp to the last texel, so the
texture unit seems to read the cache line after the one holding a
24/96-bit texel. That line is the next BO when one is mapped there
(no fault, nothing used) and an unmapped page otherwise, which depends
on the allocation order and makes the fault intermittent.

For images whose layout we choose, add 64 bytes before rounding the
data size up to a page when the (plane) format has a non-power-of-two
block size and is not compressed. That costs one page for the images
whose data ends on a page boundary and nothing for the others; explicit
(imported) layouts are unchanged.

Not proven on the hardware yet: the board A/B (old build vs this one,
kernel that names the BO around a fault) is harness/runner-queue/
46-rgb-tdim.md.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/lib/pan_layout.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_layout.c b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_layout.c
index b0114493623..7d0accbce6f 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_layout.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_layout.c
@@ -61,6 +61,19 @@ get_mip_level_extent(const struct pan_image_props *props, unsigned plane_idx,
    };
 }
 
+static bool
+pan_image_needs_overfetch_pad(enum pipe_format format, unsigned plane_idx)
+{
+   if (util_format_is_compressed(format))
+      return false;
+
+   enum pipe_format plane_format =
+      util_format_get_plane_format(format, plane_idx);
+
+   return !util_is_power_of_two_nonzero(
+      util_format_get_blocksize(plane_format));
+}
+
 bool
 pan_image_layout_init(
    unsigned arch, struct pan_image *image, unsigned plane_idx,
@@ -153,8 +166,19 @@ pan_image_layout_init(
       assert(!explicit_layout_constraints ||
              explicit_layout_constraints->offset_B ==
                 layout->slices[0].offset_B);
-      layout->data_size_B = ALIGN_POT(
-         (uint64_t)layout->array_stride_B * (uint64_t)props->array_size, 4096);
+      uint64_t size_B =
+         (uint64_t)layout->array_stride_B * (uint64_t)props->array_size;
+
+      /* Images of a non-power-of-two texel size (RGB8, RGB32) seem to be
+       * read past their last texel: on Mali-G31 such an image whose data
+       * ends on a page boundary takes a JOB_BUS_FAULT on the page-aligned VA
+       * right after the BO when nothing is mapped there. Leave one cache
+       * line of slack after these images.
+       */
+      if (pan_image_needs_overfetch_pad(props->format, plane_idx))
+         size_B += 64;
+
+      layout->data_size_B = ALIGN_POT(size_B, 4096);
    }
 
    return true;
